<!--
  Keys to add to the SiteBlock app target's Info.plist when packaging in Xcode.

  - LSUIElement makes it a menu bar app with no dock icon / no main window.
  - The app bundle identifier must be today.siteblock.SiteBlock to match the helper's
    AssociatedBundleIdentifiers / SMAuthorizedClients entries.
  - The helper daemon binary is embedded at Contents/MacOS/SiteBlockHelper and its plist at
    Contents/Library/LaunchDaemons/today.siteblock.helper.plist (see the plist template here).
-->
<key>LSUIElement</key>
<true/>

<key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
<string>today.siteblock.SiteBlock</string>

<!--
  Because the helper binds port 80 and edits /etc/hosts it runs as a privileged daemon (not a
  sandboxed XPC service). Register it from the app with:

      let service = SMAppService.daemon(plistName: "today.siteblock.helper.plist")
      try service.register()   // triggers the one-time admin approval

  The app itself enables launch-at-login via SMAppService.mainApp.register().
-->
